(1819.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHRISTIAN MYSTERY) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Commercial affaire had engaged me to make a sea voyage. I had got far) Tj T*
(from the shores of my native country, when a dreadful tempest threw me) Tj T*
(on an unknown coast; however, I fell into the hands of a very humane) Tj T*
(people, and soon found they had brought the arts to great perfection,) Tj T*
(that they practised many virtues, and appeared to me in a state as) Tj T*
(enlightened as humanity could attain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(My admiration of them equalled my gratitude, but, alas! it is but too) Tj T*
(true, that man always discovers by some failing the weakness of his) Tj T*
(being.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These people shewed as much friendship towards me as I could possibly do) Tj T*
(to them; their mildness and civility entirely gained my affection. They) Tj T*
(said to me one day, "Of what religion are you?" The question surprised) Tj T*
(me; I asked them if there were two religions, at which they smiled, and) Tj T*
(I saw they were astonished at my ignorance. "My friend," said one of) Tj T*
(them, "give thanks to God for having conducted you amongst us to be) Tj T*
(instructed in our holy religion. You do not know then that God has made) Tj T*
(himself a man?" I assured them it was the first time I had heard of it,) Tj T*
(and asked them why he had become a man? Know, continued they, that the) Tj T*
(first man eat an apple which God had forbidden him, in consequence of) Tj T*
(which all his posterity were condemned to eternal punishment. At another) Tj T*
(time men became so criminal that the Almighty repented of having created) Tj T*
(them, and drowned them all with the exception of eight persons. The) Tj T*
(posterity of these became no better, God continued to be displeased, and) Tj T*
(as it was necessary to reconcile him to mankind, God the Son became a) Tj T*
(man to appease God the Father.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This divine family astonished me a little. And the daughter of God, said) Tj T*
(I, what is become of her? They answered gravely, God has no daughter.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Oh! he has but a Son: but how do you know the sex of this Son? They) Tj T*
(answered, God is incorporeal, he has no sex. I insisted--how could God) Tj T*
(the Father produce God the Son? He begot him. God has a sex then,--he) Tj T*
(must also have a wife. They smiled at me again. But when did the Father) Tj T*
(beget this Son? From all eternity. My friends, there is an apparent) Tj T*
(contradiction, it is not possible for the Son who was begotten to be as) Tj T*
(old as the Father. Has the Father then any other children? No; but there) Tj T*
(is a third person who proceeds from the Father and the Son. I suppose) Tj T*
(he was begotten also? No; certainly not: pray take care what you say, or) Tj T*
(you will be guilty of heresy. I replied, I did not understand them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
