stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(O, Sir, these are mysteries which God himself has revealed to men, to) Tj T*
(the end that they might understand nothing. Wonderful, said I. They) Tj T*
(continued: God wished to humble men's reason, that is, to give them a) Tj T*
(disregard for the most precious gift they hold of his bounty. And you) Tj T*
(make no use of your reason then? O yes; we are allowed to use it in) Tj T*
(all other actions of our lives, but in matters of religion it would be) Tj T*
(impious. Better and better, said I. So then I find you have three Gods?) Tj T*
(No, no, replied they, we have indeed three persons, of whom the first) Tj T*
(is the Father, the second is the Son, or word, the third is the Holy) Tj T*
(Spirit; but all these three make only one God. How, Gentlemen? these) Tj T*
(three make but one, and one makes three! Yes; it is so, replied they,) Tj T*
(though contrary to all the rules of arithmetic; you must know that our) Tj T*
(theology is far superior to this petty science; however we will explain) Tj T*
(the whole to you.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What do you call the third person? said I. The Holy Ghost. Has the Holy) Tj T*
(Ghost been a man also? No; but he became a pigeon; we do not know indeed) Tj T*
(that it was his natural form, but when he appeared to the apostles he) Tj T*
(was pleased to borrow that shape.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(And the Son of God has been a man from all eternity? O no, only) Tj T*
(seventeen hundred years.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Of whom, and now was he born? He was born of a virgin. She would) Tj T*
(certainly be much surprised know-ing herself to be a virgin? O yes;) Tj T*
(you are right; but an angel came to prepare her that she might not be) Tj T*
(alarmed in being brought to bed. Yet I suppose you will be still) Tj T*
(more surprised when we tell you she was married? O no; pardon me, I) Tj T*
(understand this mystery better than all the others. Nay, do not jest,) Tj T*
(Sir, her husband had not slept with her; we have it so revealed to us.) Tj T*
(And pray how did she conceive? By the operation of the Holy Ghost. But) Tj T*
(you say that the Holy Ghost proceeds from the Son; how then could he) Tj T*
(produce the Son? Yes, Sir, it is so, by the infallible decision of the) Tj T*
(holy church. And who was his mother? The wife of a carpenter. What kind) Tj T*
(of a life did he lead? He served thirty years in his father's shop, and) Tj T*
(was very serviceable to him. Indeed, gentlemen, very well! I perceive) Tj T*
(you have sublime notions of the divinity. At the age of thirty he began) Tj T*
(to preach to the people in the country, which lasted some time; at) Tj T*
(length the magistrates became displeased, because in his sermons he) Tj T*
(said a great deal about rich men, and the officers of the government. He) Tj T*
(foresaw that he would be punished, and perspired both water and blood.) Tj T*
(Indeed! that is another fine trait in his character.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At length he was arrested by the magistrates, and crucified between two) Tj T*
(robbers. And he died? Yes. And was buried? Yes. Well then I suppose that) Tj T*
(is the end of his history? Hold, Sir, you go too fast; he died, it is) Tj T*
(true, but it was in consideration that God would pardon mankind. Oh, I) Tj T*
(understand you. God would pardon the sins of mankind because they had) Tj T*
(killed his Son. Truly, nothing could be better imagined. But know for) Tj T*
(testimony of his divinity, he rose again the third day. And what proof) Tj T*
(have you of this? The writings of his disciples. But what said the) Tj T*
(people? They contradicted it.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
