stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
() Tj T*
(Oh, gentlemen! I find you are as well provided with proofs as with) Tj T*
(reasonings; but did he perform any other miracles? Yes; he cured those) Tj T*
(possessed of evil spirits; dried a fig tree; sent devils into a herd of) Tj T*
(swine; filled the nets of his disciples with fishes, and changed water) Tj T*
(into wine; but he loved so to humble himself, that never in his life did) Tj T*
(he own that he was God. And why do you believe it? His sectaries have) Tj T*
(disputed a long time on this important article, as well as of the Holy) Tj T*
(Ghost, because three persons were not spoken of in the Old Testament.) Tj T*
(The Holy Ghost was found out to be God after twelve hundred years had) Tj T*
(passed over, and as for the divinity of Jesus, three hundred years of) Tj T*
(disputes, troubles, and massacres sufficed to decide the matter in his) Tj T*
(favour.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As you love this God so much, I suppose he was born in your country? No;) Tj T*
(he was born in another quarter of the globe. Indeed! You go very far to) Tj T*
(seek your gods! He must then have left a book of doctrines of religion,) Tj T*
(which you thought proper to adopt? No? he did not teach a new religion,) Tj T*
(neither did he write any thing; but some of his disciples have) Tj T*
(written his history and discourses. And your religion is there exactly) Tj T*
(prescribed? Oh, no! We have only a few particulars of his life,) Tj T*
(accompanied by some moral precepts; he has there declared that he) Tj T*
(came to fulfil the ancient law and not to change it. Then there was a) Tj T*
(particular religion in the country where he was born, before his time?) Tj T*
(Yes. And it is that same religion that you still observe? No; ours is) Tj T*
(in direct opposition to it. But whence then is this new religion, for) Tj T*
(you own that it was never announced by your God? We have explained,) Tj T*
(commented, interpreted without ceasing these seventeen hundred years on) Tj T*
(the discourses of Christ; and have drawn from them a long succession) Tj T*
(of dogmas and mysteries quite new. And do you all agree in these) Tj T*
(interpretations? No: far from it. We have always been disputing,) Tj T*
(fighting, and killing one another on account of them. Well, I am very) Tj T*
(sorry to tell you that I do not think your religion very attracting.) Tj T*
(What do you say? You do not agree in your explanations, and you quarrel) Tj T*
(and kill each other about them? Your religion does not at all please) Tj T*
(me; yet I suppose it had been adopted by the people of the country where) Tj T*
(your God dwelt? You are again deceived; Christ had but a very small) Tj T*
(number of disciples, and these were from the lowest class of the people.) Tj T*
(Have we not already told you that he was put to death by order of the) Tj T*
(magistrates? What do you say, gentlemen? Was not his doctrine believed) Tj T*
(by the people he attempted to instruct? No. His miracles, have they not) Tj T*
(persuaded those who were witnesses? No. And why should you believe) Tj T*
(them; you who came seventeen hundred years after him? O, Sir, all things) Tj T*
(require an explanation. Know then that God sent his Son among this) Tj T*
(people whose hearts he had hardened, purposely that they might not) Tj T*
(believe in him.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Well explained! I am quite delighted with your mode of reasoning; but) Tj T*
(pray what name do you give this people? Jews.--Jews? Jews! I never heard) Tj T*
(of them? No, I believe you. They occupied such a small territory that) Tj T*
(their reputation did not extend far; nevertheless they were formerly) Tj T*
(God's favourite people. God chose them from among all the nations of the) Tj T*
ET
